# dev-challenge

Mirror of `AGENTS.md`. Read that file for the full picture.

## Which job are you doing?

**Helping someone do a challenge.** They are learning; the code is the medium,
not the deliverable. Default to mentoring — plan with them, review their work,
name the failing acceptance criterion and explain why it fails. Do not write
the implementation unless asked. When asked, switch cleanly and say so.
Scaffolding, config and boilerplate are always fine to write outright.

**Improving the lab itself.** Normal engineering work; see `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

## The spec layer is the source of truth

`specs/` — not the code, and not `readme_files/`, which are redirect stubs.

Before answering what a challenge requires, read
`specs/challenges/<id>/spec.md` and its `acceptance.md`. The briefs disagreed
with the running API for a long time; this layer exists so that cannot recur,
and `.github/workflows/spec-drift.yml` enforces it.

Change API behaviour → update the spec and the harness test in the same commit.

## Layout

- `app/` — reference FastAPI API
- `specs/` — challenges, criteria, OpenAPI contract, design tokens
- `harness/` — black-box verifier, reports per criterion
- `scripts/` — seed, export_openapi, build_tokens, validate_specs

## Commands

```bash
ruff check app scripts tests harness
pytest --cov=app
python scripts/validate_specs.py
python harness/cli.py --base-url http://localhost:3000 --challenge backend-05-balance
```

## Conventions

- Primary button `#19191C` (near-black), not purple. Purple is brand surfaces.
  Import `specs/design/tokens.css` rather than hard-coding hex.
- Credit `#0CB97B`, debit `#E02244`; colour is never the only signal — keep the
  sign and the arrow.
- Web and mobile specs declare `testids`; the harness drives the UI through
  them.
- Balances and statement lists are per user (`from_user` / `to_user` match on
  full name). The global ledger is the commonest back-end mistake.
- Mobile tokens in Keychain/Keystore, never `AsyncStorage`/`UserDefaults`.
- Never commit a secret. `app/.env` is git-ignored.
- Ruff, 100 columns, Conventional Commits. Comments explain *why*.

